  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "A question-and-answer contest between Othin and the giant Vafthruthnir covers cosmogony (world made from Ymir), origins of sun, moon, day, night, seasons, the giants’ beginnings and reproduction, Bergelmir borne in a boat, the source of wind, Njorth’s origin as a pledge between divine groups, daily battle and healing of the heroes in Othin’s hall, the speaker’s travel to nine worlds including Niflhel, survival of Lif and Lifthrasir in Hoddmimir’s wood during a mighty winter, and the sun’s continuation through a daughter after Fenrir seizes it. The passage ends with Othin asking about maidens who will fare over the sea (answer not included).",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir says the earth was fashioned from Ymir’s flesh, mountains from his bones, the sky from his skull, and the ocean from his blood.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir says Mundilferi begat the moon and fathered the sun, and that the sun and moon run their courses to tell time for men.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir says Day’s father is Delling and Night was begotten by Nor, and that full moon and old moon were fashioned by the gods to tell time for men.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir says Vindsval fathered winter and Svosuth begat summer.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir names Bergelmir as the first/earliest remembered giant and gives his lineage (son of Thruthgelmir, grandson of Aurgelmir).",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir says venom dropped down from Elivagar and waxed until it became a giant, from which the giants’ race arose.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir reports that under the arms of the ice giant, a man-child and maid grew together, and that the giant’s feet fashioned a son with six heads.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir says he first knew of Bergelmir when the wise giant was borne in a boat of old.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir says Hrsvelg sits in an eagle’s guise at the end of heaven and that wind comes from his wings to move over the world of men.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir says Njorth was created in the home of the Wanes and given as a pledge to the gods, and at the world’s fall will return home to the Wanes.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir says the heroes in Othin’s hall fight each day, fell each other, and return from the fight healed soon to sit.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Vafthruthnir says he can tell the truth of the runes of gods and giants and that he has come to nine worlds, including to Niflhel beneath where dead men dwell.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "Asked what shall live of mankind when a mighty winter comes, Vafthruthnir says Lif and Lifthrasir will hide in Hoddmimir’s wood and have morning dew for meat.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "Asked whence the sun comes back when Fenrir has snatched it forth, Vafthruthnir says Alfrothul bears a bright daughter before this, and the maiden will tread her mother’s paths after the gods have gone to death.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "Othin asks what maidens, wise of mind, will fare over the sea; the passage ends before Vafthruthnir’s answer appears.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:15"
      ]
    }
