    "summary": "Editor/translator notes identify and gloss figures and plot points referenced in stanzas 46–55: Fenrir vs. Skoll (who steals the sun), the sun-name Alfrothul, Mogthrasir, maidens interpreted as kindly Norns, Surt, Othin’s sons (including Vithar who kills Fenrir and Vali who avenges Baldr), Thor’s sons (Mothi and Magni) inheriting Mjollnir after Thor’s death, an unanswerable question about what Othin whispered to Baldr at the funeral pyre leading the giant to recognize his guest, and the giant Vafthruthnir’s head-wager in a wisdom contest implying death upon defeat.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
