  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Editorial notes summarizing and cross-referencing episodes and details from Harbarthsljoth and related Eddic material: Valland (Land of Slaughter) and the taking of slain heroes to Othin; Thor’s eastward journey and the giant Skrymir/Utgartha-Loki whose glove serves as a house; a boundary river (Ifing) between gods and giants; idiomatic terms (\"heel-biter\"); Hlesey and berserkers as bear-shifters; identifications of figures related to Thor (Thjalfi, Sif, Magni, Thor’s mother Earth/Fjorgyn); Othin’s seeking information from the dead by magic; and the rainbow bridge Bifrost as a road.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
