      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "The introductory note describes the poem as primarily consisting of Loki's taunts to assembled gods and goddesses, and notes that the prose sections fill narrative gaps like stage directions and include an account of Loki's punishment.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Ægir (also called Gymir) prepares ale for a feast of the gods; many named gods and beings are listed as attending, while Thor is absent on a journey in the East.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Tyr is described as having one hand because the wolf Fenrir bit off the other hand when Fenrir was bound.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Ægir has two serving-men, Fimafeng and Eldir; the hall is lit by glittering gold instead of firelight, and the ale comes in of itself.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Loki kills the serving-man Fimafeng; the gods shake their shields, howl at Loki, and drive him away to the forest, then resume drinking.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Outside the hall Loki speaks with Eldir, asking what the gods are talking about; Eldir replies they talk of weapons and war and that Loki will find no friend in words among the gathered gods and elves.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Loki declares he will go into Ægir's hall, bringing \"bale and hatred\" and mixing venom into their mead; Eldir warns him the gods may wipe slander back on him.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "When Loki enters the hall, those present fall silent; Loki says he is thirsty and asks for mead, and demands a seat or to be told to leave.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
