  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Rig visits three households in sequence. Each time he sits with the couple, sleeps between them for three nights, then departs; after nine months a son is born, sprinkled with water, and named. The first household produces Thrall (with a wife Thir and many children), associated with hard labor and the origin of thralls. The second produces Karl (who marries Snor and has many children), associated with farming and building and the origin of yeomen. The third produces Jarl, wrapped in silk and described as fair and intense-eyed, born in a wealthier hall with fine food, wine, and silver-covered vessels.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Rig stays in a home for three nights, then goes onward; nine months later a child is born.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1",
        "ev:2",
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Newborn sons are sprinkled with water at birth and named (Thrall, Karl, Jarl).",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4",
        "ev:5",
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Thrall is physically described as wrinkled-skinned and rough-handed, with knotted knuckles and an ugly face; he grows strong and performs heavy carrying and binding work.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Thrall takes Thir as partner; they whisper, prepare a bed, and later have many named sons and daughters who do household and farm labor (dunging ground, guarding swine, tending goats, digging turf).",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Rig comes to a hall owned by Afi and Amma; a fire is on the floor; the man hews wood and the woman works with a distaff and weaving.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Amma serves food including boiled calf's flesh; Rig speaks wise words, then sleeps in the bed with the others on either side.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Karl grows strong; he rules oxen, readies plows, builds houses and barns, and makes carts.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "A bride is brought for Karl; she is clad in goatskins, bears keys, is named Snor, and rings are exchanged; their children are listed and are said to be the origin of the yeomen's race.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Rig enters a hall whose doors face south; the portal stands wide and a ring is on the posts; the floor is strewn.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "In the third hall, Fathir and Mothir gaze at each other and play with their fingers; the house-lord makes bows and shafts; the lady wears fine clothing and jewelry and is described as very fair.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Mothir brings a broidered linen cloth, thin wheat loaves, silver-covered vessels, browned meat, well-cooked birds, wine in a pitcher, and plated cups; they drink and talk until day is gone.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Jarl is wrapped in silk, sprinkled with water, is blond and bright-cheeked, and has glowing eyes described as 'grim as a snake's'.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    }
