  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Jarl grows up training in martial skills. Rig arrives from a grove, teaches him runes, calls him by name, and claims him as a son, instructing him to hold a broad heritage. Jarl rides out, makes war, wins land, and comes to hold many halls; he gains wealth and distributes gifts. His messengers seek a bride from a man named Hersir; Jarl marries Erna and they have many sons, including Kon the Young. Kon learns powerful runes and abilities (including understanding bird-speech and affecting fire, minds, and the sea). Kon shares runes with Rig-Jarl and earns the right to be called Rig. Riding out, Kon hears a crow speak, advising him that it would be better to ride forth to slay a host; the crow points to the noble halls and wealth of Dan and Danp and praises their skills.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
