    "summary": "Svipdag calls to his dead mother Groa from the doors of the dead, asking for protective charms before a dangerous journey compelled by a hostile woman. Groa rises to speak and chants a sequence of spells to protect him from misfortune, restraints, storms, cold, curses, enemies, and verbal contest, then sends him forth with a blessing that her words will endure in him.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
