  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Svipdag arrives at a giant hall surrounded by fire and is confronted by Fjolsvith, who denies him entry and questions his identity. Svipdag asks a series of questions about the hall’s ruler, its gate and house, a great tree, a shining cock on the tree, and two guard-hounds that prevent entry by alternating their sleep. Fjolsvith explains how the hounds might be distracted with meat taken from the cock’s body, and describes a weapon (Lvatein) made with runes by the ‘doors of death’ and kept in a locked chest guarded by Sinmora. To obtain the weapon, one must bring a treasure to Sinmora: a bright sickle found among the cock’s feathers.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
