        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Svipdag’s stepmother is described as responsible for his search for Mengloth; the name Mengloth is noted as suggesting identification with Frigg or Freyja (as possessor of a famous necklace).",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "A catalogue of charms is noted; the notes mention figures Rind and Rani in connection with Othin and the begetting of Vali as avenger of Baldr.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Urth is identified as one of the three Norns (Fates).",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Two rivers (Horn and Ruth) are described as symbolizing dangerous streams in general.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "The notes discuss a charm involving a dead Christian woman’s curse and explain that conservative pagans could regard Christians as emissaries of darkness; a dead woman’s curse is described as more potent than a living one’s.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "A prose link is proposed: after Groa’s song ends, Svipdag goes to seek Mengloth and comes to a great house surrounded by flames with a giant standing before it.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "The giant Fjolsvith is described as warder of the house where Mengloth dwells; he sees Svipdag coming and stops him with threats.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "A gate named Thrymgjol is described as shutting so fast as to trap those who attempt to use it; it was made by dwarfs, sons of Solblindi, described as craftsmen who could not endure daylight.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Gastropnir is glossed as 'Guest-Crusher'; 'Leirbrimir’s limbs' are described as a circumlocution for clay.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Mimameith is identified as the ash Yggdrasil which overshadows the whole world; the well of Mimir is said to be at its base, and the fruit of Yggdrasil when cooked is assumed to assure safe childbirth.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Vithofnir is glossed as 'Tree-Snake' and associated with a watchfulness that terrifies giants; Sinmora is described as possessing the weapon by which alone Vithofnir may be slain.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "A chain of requirements is described: to get past the dogs, they must be fed with the wing-joints of the cock Vithofnir; the cock can be killed only with the sword in Sinmora’s possession; Sinmora will give up the sword only in return for the tail feather of the cock.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "Lvatein is glossed as 'Wounding Wand'; Lopt and the 'Lover of Ill' are identified as Loki; a suggestion connecting Lvatein to the mistletoe that killed Baldr is described as hardly reasonable.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "The hall’s glowing brightness is said to make it seem to quiver and turn in the air, and the tradition is described as possibly balancing the whole building on a single point (a spear-point reference is mentioned).",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:15"
      ]
    }
