  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Vlund repairs a gold object and brings beer so that Bothvild soon sleeps. He declares that he has taken vengeance for his injuries. He rises aloft laughing, while Bothvild weeps and leaves the isle. Nithuth, grieving for his slain sons, asks to speak with Vlund and demands to know what happened to them. Vlund requires Nithuth to swear multiple oaths, then reveals he killed Nithuth's two sons, hid parts of their bodies in the smithy, and fashioned treasures from their skulls, eyes, and teeth, giving these items to Nithuth, Nithuth's wife, and Bothvild. He states Bothvild is now pregnant. Nithuth says Vlund cannot be captured while he travels in the clouds. Nithuth then questions Bothvild, who confirms she was with Vlund on the isle and says she could not resist his strength.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Vlund says he will weld a break in gold so well that it will seem fairer and better, and the object will be no worse than before.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Beer is brought, and a woman (contextually Bothvild) soon sleeps in her seat.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Vlund states he now has vengeance for all his hurts except one on an 'evil woman,' and he references the sinews in his feet being maimed by Nithuth's men.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Vlund rises aloft laughing; Bothvild weeps and goes from the isle, for her lover's flight and her father's wrath.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Nithuth is described as waking always and joyless since his sons were slain; he wishes to speak with Vlund and asks what happened to his boys.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Vlund demands Nithuth swear oaths by the rail of ship, rim of shield, shoulder of steed, and edge of sword, promising not to harm Vlund's wife or bride, even if he has a wife known to Nithuth and a child within Nithuth's hall.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Vlund says Nithuth will find the bellows sprinkled with blood; Vlund says he struck off the heads of both Nithuth's sons and hid their feet beneath sooty straps.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Vlund says he took the sons' skulls, set them in silver, and sent them to Nithuth; he fashioned gems from their eyes and gave them to Nithuth's wife; he made a brooch from their teeth and gave it to Bothvild.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Vlund states Bothvild is 'big with child' and is the only daughter Nithuth and his wife had.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Nithuth says there is no man high enough to take Vlund from his horse nor archer strong enough to shoot him down while he takes his course high in the clouds.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Nithuth orders the thrall Thakkrath to bring Bothvild, bedecked, to speak with her father; Nithuth asks Bothvild if it is true she was once in the isle with Vlund.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Bothvild confirms she was once in the isle with Vlund for 'an hour of lust' and says she had no might against such a man and could not save herself from his strength.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    }
