  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "After Helgi has slain multiple enemies, a radiant, martial scene is described. In a wooded meeting, Sigrun (Hogni's daughter) tells Helgi she has been pledged as bride to Hothbrodd (Granmar's son) and urges Helgi to confront him or take her. Helgi sends messengers to gather men and ships; the fleet assembles and sails amid clash of iron and threatening sea-beings, while Sigrun aids their voyage. The fleet arrives and is observed from a hill. A verbal exchange follows between Gothmund and Sinfjotli, featuring boasts and insults, including accusations of wolfish cannibalism, witchcraft/valkyrie identity, and a claim of gelding by giant-women.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "A king sits after having slain Eyjolf and Alf, and also Hjorvarth and Hovarth, described as Hunding's sons; he has killed the kin of the spear-wielder.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Light glitters from Logafjoll; flashes leap from the light; armed figures are described with helms, blood-red byrnies, and sparks flying from spears (with lacunae in the text).",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "In \"wolf-wood\" the mighty king asks a southern maid whether she will come home with the hero that night; weapons clash.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Hogni's daughter (Sigrun) springs down from her horse and speaks to the hero, saying they have other tasks than drinking beer with the \"breaker of rings.\"",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Sigrun states her father has pledged her as bride to Hothbrodd, Granmar's son; she insults Hothbrodd by comparison and says he will come soon unless Helgi bids him seek the battlefield or takes the maid from the warrior.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Helgi tells her not to fear and says their courage must be tried; he implies weapons will clash unless he dies.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Helgi sends messengers by land and sea to seek a host, wealth, and to summon men; he orders them to seek the ships and be ready off Brandey, and he waits for men arriving by hundreds.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Ships stand off Stafnsnes, described as fair and adorned with gold; Helgi asks Hjorleif if he has counted the host; Hjorleif speaks of long-stemmed ships with warriors coming into Orvasund and mentions numbers of men and the king's host in Hotun.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "The chieftain strikes the ship-tents, wakes the warriors, and the men fasten sails on the masts in Varinsfjord; oars beat, iron clashes, shield smites shield, and the fleet goes forth from land.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "The sound of keels striking is likened to cliffs broken by beating surf; Helgi orders higher sails; \"girs daughters\" seek to sink the sea-steeds (ships) but Sigrun from above aids the men and their voyage; a sea-beast is mentioned in connection with \"the claws of Ron.\"",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "At evening in Unavagar the fleet floats bedecked; observers from Svarins hill see the host and are bitter at heart.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Gothmund asks who the monarch is that guides the host; Sinfjotli answers, raises a red shield with a golden rim while on an oar, and is described as a sea-sentry skilled in speech and contention with princes.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "Sinfjotli taunts the others with insults about feeding swine and claims the Ylfings have come from the East to Gnipalund; he says Hothbrodd will find Helgi in the midst of the fleet and notes Helgi has often gorged eagles.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "Gothmund rebukes Sinfjotli, accuses him of eating wolves' entrails and being the slayer of his brothers, sucking wounds, and lurking in rocky dens.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "Sinfjotli accuses Gothmund of being a witch on Varins isle, false and a maker of lies, and calls him a valkyrie/witch in Allfather's home whose subtlety causes warriors to fight; he claims they had nine wolf-cubs in Sogunes and that he was their father (with lacunae nearby).",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:16",
      "text": "Gothmund denies Sinfjotli fathered Fenrir's wolves and claims Sinfjotli was gelded in Gnipalund by giant-women at Thorsnes.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:16"
      ]
    }
