      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Messengers (Sviputh and Sveggjuth) run to Solheimar and find the king at his courtyard gate to report that a fierce foe has come.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Gothmund reports a large host arriving by ships, giving numbers of bands landed and men out in Sogn.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "There are ships at anchor off Gnipalund described as \"fire-beasts\" and fitted with gold; the enemy men wait there and Helgi will not delay battle.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Hothbrodd orders horses to be readied and calls for allies and warriors to go against the Volsungs.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "At Frekastein, flashing blades clash; Helgi is described as first in the throng and fierce in battle.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Helmed maidens come from heaven and watch over the king during the battle; Sigrun speaks.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Sigrun hails Helgi as a hero, calls him offspring of Yngvi, and says he has slain a fearless foe who brought dread of death to many.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Sigrun says Helgi has won red rings and a noble bride, identified as Hogni's daughter, along with Hringstathir, wealth, and triumph as the battle wanes.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
