  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "A quarrel of insulting speech is followed by prose narration in which Helgi marries Sigrun but is killed when Dag (Sigrun’s brother) sacrifices to Othin for vengeance and receives a spear from him. Sigrun curses Dag, who offers compensation. Helgi is memorialized with a hill (burial mound); in Valhall Othin assigns Helgi authority, and Helgi orders the slain Hunding to serve. Later a maiden sees dead men riding to Helgi’s mound; Sigrun goes there and meets Helgi, who is cold, frost-covered, and wounded. They drink in the mound among other dead heroes and their brides; Sigrun prepares a bed and sleeps clasped in the arms of the corpse, and Helgi warns that events may follow from her sleeping with a corpse.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "A speaker mocks Gothmund, saying it would be better for him to tend goats and climb mountain cliffs than hold a sword.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Helgi rebukes Sinfjotli, saying it would be better for him to give battles and gladden eagles than to utter empty speech.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Helgi takes Sigrun as wife and they have sons; Helgi does not reach old age.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Dag, son of Hogni, offers sacrifice to Othin to be avenged for his father's death, and Othin gives Dag a spear.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Dag finds Helgi at Fjoturlund and thrusts the spear through Helgi’s body; Helgi falls.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Dag rides to Sevafjoll and tells Sigrun that Helgi has fallen at Fjoturlund.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2",
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Sigrun calls for Dag’s oaths to bite him, invoking the bright water of Leipt and the ice-cold stone of Uth.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Sigrun pronounces a curse that Dag’s ship will not sail and his horse will not run; she also says his sword shall not bite until it sings about his own head.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Dag says Sigrun is mad to cast such a curse, and states that Othin is ruler of every ill and sunders kin with runes of spite.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Dag offers Sigrun rings, named lands (Vandilsve and Vigdalir), and half his land as compensation and as meed for her sons.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Sigrun says she cannot sit happy at Sevafjoll if she cannot see Helgi brought back home, naming a golden-bitted bearer (Vigblar).",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Helgi’s foes are said to have feared him as goats run from a wolf among the rocks; Helgi is compared to a lofty ash above thorns and to a noble stag whose horns gleam to heaven.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "A hill is made in Helgi’s memory; when Helgi comes to Valhall, Othin bids him rule over everything with himself.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "In Valhall, Helgi orders Hunding to wash the feet of heroes, kindle the fire, and tend animals.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "One evening, a maiden goes to Helgi’s hill and sees Helgi riding to the hill with many men; she wonders whether it is a dream or whether dead men ride and home-coming is granted to heroes.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:16",
      "text": "Helgi tells the maiden it is not a dream and not the end of the world, and says home-coming is not granted to the heroes though they are seen riding there.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:17",
      "text": "The maiden tells Sigrun that the hill is open and Helgi is come; she says the sword-tracks bleed and that Helgi bade Sigrun make his wounds well.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:18",
      "text": "Sigrun goes into the hill to Helgi, says she is glad of the meeting, and kisses the lifeless king; she notes frost-heavy hair, the dew of death, and ice-cold hands.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:19",
      "text": "Helgi says Sigrun’s tears fall like blood on his breast and that he is heavy with dew because of her; he says they will drink a noble draught in the hill though love and lands are lost, and states that in the hill they hold their brides, the heroes’ loves, by their husbands dead.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8",
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:20",
      "text": "Sigrun makes ready a bed in the hill and says she will make Helgi sleep in her arms as when he was living; Helgi remarks that something may happen since she sleeps clasped in a corpse’s arms though she comes living.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    }
