    "summary": "A speaker describes riding a horse along “reddened ways” and treading the sky toward bridges before a figure named Salgofnir wakes the warrior host. Helgi and his followers depart, while Sigrun has a maiden watch at a hill. At sunset Sigrun laments Helgi’s absence and hopes for his return from Odin’s seat, mentioning eagles on ash-tree boughs and men seeking “the meeting of dreams.” The maiden warns Sigrun that seeking the house of the dead alone seems mad, since ghosts are mightier at night. Sigrun later dies of sorrow, and the note reports an old belief in rebirth, stating that Helgi and Sigrun were born again as Helgi Haddingjaskati and Kara (a valkyrie), daughter of Halfdan.",
