  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "In dialogue, Sigurth repeatedly asks the seer Gripir to tell his future life. Gripir foretells that Sigurth will find Fafnir's lair and treasure, take the gold on his horse Grani, and go to Gjuki. He foretells that Sigurth will awaken an armored maiden sleeping on rocks (Brynhild) by cutting her mail-coat; she will teach him runes and languages. Gripir also foretells that Sigurth's death is doomed, that he will be deceived by Grimhild into shifting plans and oaths, and that Sigurth will take Gunnar's form to win Brynhild's hand for Gunnar while keeping his own mind and voice.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
