    "summary": "Sigurth chooses the horse Grani and is fostered by the dwarf Regin, who recounts how the gods killed Otr (in otter form) and were forced to pay ransom by filling and covering the otter-skin with gold taken from Andvari (a dwarf in pike form). Loki seizes Andvari’s ring, and Andvari and Loki speak of curses and future strife. Hreithmar receives the gold, but his son Fafnir kills him and takes the hoard; Regin is denied inheritance and later urges Sigurth to slay Fafnir, now a dragon with a fear-helm. Regin forges the sword Gram for Sigurth, who first seeks to avenge his father; Hjalprek gives him a fleet, and they meet a storm as a man stands on a mountain and speaks.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
