      "evidence_refs": ["ev:1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Regin, son of Hreithmar, arrives at Hjalpreks home; he is described as ingenious, dwarf in stature, wise, fierce, and skilled in magic; he undertakes Sigurths upbringing and teaching.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Regin recounts that Othin, Hnir, and Loki come to Andvaris waterfall; Andvari is a dwarf living there in the shape of a pike.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Otr (Regin’s brother) often goes into the waterfall in the shape of an otter; Loki kills him with a stone; the gods strip the otter-skin as booty.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "At Hreithmars house the gods are seized and required, as ransom for their lives, to fill the otter skin with gold and cover it outside with red gold.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Loki uses Ron’s net to catch the pike (Andvari) in the waterfall; Loki and Andvari exchange speeches identifying Andvari and referencing a doom to dwell in waters; Loki takes a ring that Andvari tries to hold back.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Andvari goes into a rocky hole and declares that the gold will bring death and evil; later the gods fill and cover the otter-skin with gold, and Othin uses the ring Andvaranaut to cover a remaining whisker.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:4"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Fafnir and Regin ask Hreithmar for a share of the wealth paid for Otr; Hreithmar refuses; Fafnir kills his sleeping father with a sword and takes all the gold; Regin is later refused inheritance by Fafnir.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:5"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Regin seeks counsel from his sister Lyngheith on how to win his inheritance; she advises asking in friendly wise rather than taking with the sword.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:6"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Regin tells Sigurth that Fafnir lies at Gnitaheith in the shape of a dragon and has a fear-helm that terrifies living creatures.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:7"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Regin makes for Sigurth the sword Gram; it is tested by cleaving drifting wool in the Rhine and by Sigurth cleaving Regins anvil.",
