      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Hnikar lists signs good for fighting: meeting a black raven on the road; seeing two fighters greedy of fame on the path before one's house; hearing a howling wolf under the ash; and seeing one's foe before the foe sees the hero.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Hnikar warns against fighting when one must face \"the moons bright sister\" setting late, and says the one who can see well and form men in wedge-like shapes will win.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Hnikar says stumbling when going forth to fight is a foul sign, and that baneful goddesses at both sides will cause wounds.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Hnikar advises that the wise man should be combed and washed, take a morning meal, and not lose luck because it is unknown where he may be at evening.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Sigurth has a great battle with Lyngvi, son of Hunding, and Lyngvi and his two brothers fall there.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "After the battle, Regin says that the \"bloody eagle\" is carved with biting sword on the back of Sigmund's killer, and refers to reddening the earth and gladdening the ravens.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Sigurth goes home to Hjalprek's house, and Regin eggs him on to fight with Fafnir.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    }
