    "summary": "Editorial notes discuss manuscript and saga variants around Fafnir’s death: Sigurth’s trench dug to avoid harm from the dragon’s blood/venom, an old man identified as Othin advising additional trenches, and multiple cross-references to other Eddic poems and the Volsungasaga (including possible interpolations, missing lines, and stanza rearrangements). Additional notes gloss mythic figures (Norns, Dvalin, Surt), items (fear-helm, Gram), and kennings/proverbs (e.g., “tree of battle”).",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "The notes state that in the Volsungasaga, blood (not venom) pours down on Sigurth’s head, and Sigurth worries about this danger before digging the trench.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Regin taunts Sigurth with cowardice when Sigurth asks what would happen if the dragon’s blood overcomes him; the stanza containing the taunt is said to have disappeared, though Sigurth refers to it later (stanza 30).",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1",
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "After Sigurth digs his trench, an old man (identified in the notes as Othin) appears and advises him to dig additional trenches to carry off the blood, which Sigurth does, thereby escaping harm.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "The notes describe some stanzas (11–15) as probably interpolated and coming from a poem similar to Vafthruthnismol; they are described as proverb-like and paraphrased in the Volsungasaga.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "The notes mention Norns (including ‘minor Norns’ besides three great Norns) and identify Dvalin as chief of the dwarfs.",
