      "text": "The introductory note states that a long poem in Codex Regius bears the heading Sigurtharkvitha but is referred to as the short Lay of Sigurth in a prose link; it discusses conjectures about length, interpolations, and omissions.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "The introductory note states the poet uses narrative as background for characterization, and that lyric elements overshadow epic elements; it mentions confusions of narrative tradition.",
