  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Warriors discuss trying to prevent a queen from dying, but Hogni says she cannot be kept from death and was born for wicked deeds. Gunnar turns away while the jewel-bearer divides her treasures and looks over slain bond-women and slaves. The woman puts on a gold byrnie, pierces herself with a sword, and speaks further: she offers gifts, declines to force unwilling women to die with her, and foretells events involving Gunnar, Guthrun, Atli, Oddrun, Jonak, and Svanhild, including killings and vengeance. She requests a broad funeral pyre, to be covered with shields and textiles, and that slaves, animals, and others be burned; she asks that a sharp sword lie between herself and her mate as before. Her voice weakens as she dies.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Warriors in a hall are urged to come forth and try to hold the queen from death until her fearful thoughts fade.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Hogni says they cannot hold her from the long road and that she cannot be born again; he states she came foul from her mother and was born for wicked deeds, bringing sorrow to many.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Gunnar turns gloomily away while the jewel-bearer divides her gems and looks on her wealth, and on slain bond-women and slaughtered slaves.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "The woman dons a gold byrnie and pierces herself with the point of her sword; she lays her head on a pillow and ponders her plan while wounded.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "She calls for women who desire gold, offering necklaces, cloth, and bright garments; those present answer that enough are slain and they seek to live.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "She says that for her sake none unwilling or loath to die shall lay down her life; she warns they will find little gems when they fare forth to follow her.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "She addresses Gunnar and speaks of his bride and her desire to die; she foretells Guthrun's later mourning and subsequent marriage, and that Guthrun will bring woe to many warriors.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "She foretells that Atli will seek Guthrun, and recalls being treated with betrayal and treacherous wiles.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "She foretells a secret love-tryst between Gunnar and Oddrun, which Atli withholds publicly.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "She foretells that Atli will cast Gunnar down in a den of snakes, and later Guthrun will kill Atli with a blade in his bed; she also says Atli will lose fortune and the lives of his sons.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "She foretells Guthrun will not lose her life but will wander over tossing waves to Jonak's realm, bear him sons, and that Svanhild (Sigurth's child) will be sent far away; Bikki's word will cause Svanhild's death through the wrath of Jormunrek, and all of Sigurth's race will be slain.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "She asks as a last boon that a broad pyre be built in the field with room for all slain with Sigurth; she asks that it be covered with shields and carpets (and other textiles), and that fallen slaves be included.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "She specifies that slaves should burn, with two at the head and two at the feet, along with a brace of hounds and a pair of hawks, so that all will be seemly done.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "She asks that the keen steel lie between her and her mate once more, as when they were in one bed and called wedded mates.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "She says bond-women and thralls, including children, will follow him; she states these were gifts Buthli gave his daughter.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:16",
      "text": "She says her voice grows weak and her wounds swell; she says she has spoken truth and dies.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    }
  ],
