      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Brynhild says from the wagon she will tell how the heirs of Gjuki made her joyless and a breaker of oaths.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Brynhild says she was named Hild the helmed in Hlymdalir and that a monarch bore the swan-robes of eight sisters beneath an oak; she says she was twelve winters old when she yielded oaths to a young king.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Brynhild says she caused Hjalmgunnar the old to go down to hell and brought victory to Autha’s brother, which provoked Othin’s mighty anger.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Brynhild says Othin beset her with overlapping red and white shields in Skatalund and decreed her sleep would be broken by one who had nowhere found fear.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Brynhild says Othin made high-leaping fire burn around her southward-looking hall and bade the hero come across it—he who brought her the gold that Fafnir guarded.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "A stanza states that a figure rode on Grani and is called the giver of gold; he went where Brynhild’s foster-father ruled, and he appeared the best when people met.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "Brynhild says she and Sigurth slept in one bed as if he were her brother, and for eight nights neither laid a loving hand on the other.",
      "category": "relationship",
