  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "An envoy announces Atli’s invitation to Gunnar with promises of weapons, wealth, lands, and other gifts. Gunnar and Hogni discuss the offer; Hogni interprets a ring woven with a wolf’s hair as a warning. Despite reluctance among companions, Gunnar departs with a following and rides through Myrkwood to Atli’s halls. Their sister warns Gunnar inside the hall that he is betrayed and urges him to flee, predicting a fate in a snake-den. Gunnar says it is too late to summon allies; he is seized and chained. Hogni fights, killing several foes and throwing one into a fire. Gunnar is offered the chance to buy his life with gold, but demands the heart of Hogni as proof; the captors first cut out Hjalli’s heart, which Gunnar recognizes as cowardly, and then cut out Hogni’s heart while Hogni laughs.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
