      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Gunnar states that he knows of no gold on Gnitaheith so fair that they do not already have its equal; he lists his own halls, weapons, armor, and helmet as superior to Hun treasure.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Hogni interprets a ring sent to them—woven with a wolf’s hair—as a warning, noting a hair in the red ring and saying their road will be wolf-like if they ride.",
