      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Atli rides a long-maned horse named Glaum with warriors around him; Guthrun does not yield to tears in the hall.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Guthrun invokes oaths sworn by the sun, by Sigtyr's mountain, by the horse of the rest-bed, and by the ring of Ull.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Gunnar is cast alive into a den where serpents crawl; he strikes the harp-strings with his hand and the strings resound.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Atli returns home from the slaughter-place; there is clatter of hoofs and clashing of arms in the court.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Guthrun meets Atli with a golden beaker and tells him he may eat within his dwelling, mentioning fresh-slaughtered young beasts.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Guthrun tells Atli that he has eaten the hearts of his sons in honey and the flesh of the slain, and that he will never again call to his knees Erp or Eitil.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "There is clamor and weeping among the Huns; Guthrun does not weep, neither for her brothers nor for the boys she had with Atli.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Guthrun scatters gold and gives red-gold rings to followers, and does not spare the treasure of the temple.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "Atli is described as unwise and drunk, weaponless, and not wary of Guthrun.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "Guthrun takes vengeance by using her sword to give blood for the bed to drink, loosing hounds, awakening thralls, and throwing a firebrand in the hall door.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "Those inside are given to the flames; timbers fall, the temple and dwelling burn, and shield-maids burn and die in the hot flames.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:16",
      "text": "The narration claims no later woman in byrnie will avenge her brothers so, and that she brought death-doom to three kings before she died.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:16"
      ]
