    "summary": "Hogni is seized and faces death laughing. Gunnar plays a harp with his toes, moving listeners. Atli blames Guthrun for the loss of her loved ones and offers compensation, but she refuses and recalls her brothers. Guthrun deceives Atli and prepares a feast. She kills Atli’s two sons, then reveals to Atli that he drank from their skulls as cups, that their blood was mixed into his drink, and that he ate their cooked hearts. Atli reacts with grief and threatens punishment; Guthrun answers defiantly.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
