      "text": "Guthrun calls Atli a liar and says he was cruel; she describes brothers who fought, many sons of his house going to hell, and things being destroyed; she recounts that she and her two brothers went forth with Sigurth, sailed east, slew a king, seized land, and made many rich; she says after the Hun-king was slain happiness vanished and the widow wept, and that coming to Atli’s house was worse sorrow after losing her heroic husband.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Atli asks Guthrun to be kindly once more for the honor of both when he is borne forth (carried out dead).",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Guthrun promises to buy a ship and a bright-hued coffin, to wax the shroud to wrap his body, and to care for all as if they had been dear.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Atli dies; Guthrun does as promised; she then seeks to go to her death, but waits for days and it is long before she dies.",
