    "summary": "Editorial notes on stanzas 90–98 of Atlamol en Grnllenzku discussing manuscript issues, speaker uncertainties, and interpretive points: Atli’s reproach of Guthrun about conflict with his brothers and the claim to Sigurth’s hoard; references to the Volsungasaga and to the historical Attila; a note that Atli’s mother appears elsewhere as an adder that stings Gunnar; mention of a maritime expedition described as poetic invention; outlawed men restored; Atli depicted as a Norse land-owner attending the Thing; and a note about ship burial and the (already killed) heirs of Atli.",
