    "summary": "A princess and her nurse suspect a man is the deposed king Jemshd, but he denies his identity despite their appeals and a portrait used as evidence. He explains he fears a powerful enemy and does not trust women with secrets, but eventually confesses and recounts his misfortunes. The princess marries him privately. Her father King Greng discovers the marriage through spies; after the nurse cites a prophecy and destiny that the princess will soon be a mother, Greng feigns satisfaction, planning to betray Jemshd by sending him bound to Zohk in hopes of a reward.",
