      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "When shown a picture as evidence, the man answers that he might resemble Jemshd and that two men can look alike.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "The princess states a nurse has foretold she would be united to Jemshd and bear him a son; she says she has rejected other kings because she is destined for him.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "The man gives two reasons for concealing the truth: he has a powerful enemy who must not learn his refuge, and he does not entrust secrets to a woman.",
