    "quote": "",
    "summary": "King Zohk dreams of being attacked, struck, bound, and dragged before crowds. Court wise men interpret the dream as a prophecy that Zohk will fall and that Feridn (not yet born) will succeed him and avenge his father's blood. Zohk orders persecution of the relevant family; Feridn's father Abtn is captured and executed. Feridn's mother Farnuk flees with the infant, whose nursing is sustained by milk from a cow (Pur'mieh) after the mother's milk dries up; the child is left with a pasture-keeper for three years, then moved toward refuge on Mount Alberz by the mother's divinely inspired impulse. Zohk later kills the keeper, his tribe, and the cow, but fails to find Feridn. A dervish on Mount Alberz fosters Feridn and teaches him; he tells the mother that her son is foretold to destroy Zohk and become monarch.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Zohk dreams of three warriors attacking him; the youngest strikes his head with a mace, binds his hands, puts a rope around his neck, and drags him before crowds.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Zohk consults the Mbids (wise men) for a dream interpretation; they delay out of fear, then state that Zohk's life nears its end and that Feridn, though unborn, will succeed him and strike him, seeking vengeance for his father's blood spilled by Zohk.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Feridn's parents are named Abtn (father) and Farnuk (mother), and Farnuk is said to be of the race of Tahmers; Zohk orders members of the family of the Kais seized; Abtn is recognized by spies, taken to Zohk, and executed.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Farnuk flees with her two-month-old infant; her milk dries up from grief, and the infant is fed with milk from a cow named Pur'mieh belonging to a pasture-keeper; Farnuk leaves Feridn with the keeper and goes to Mount Alberz.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "The pasture-keeper raises Feridn for three years; Farnuk returns secretly to retrieve Feridn and move him to a safer refuge on Mount Alberz, stating that God inspired her to remove him.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "After learning Feridn was protected by the pasture-keeper, Zohk comes with a large force, kills the keeper, his tribe, and the cow, destroys the dwelling, and cannot find Feridn.",
