    "summary": "Zohk convenes nobles and proposes raising an army and creating an annual muster-roll. Kavah the blacksmith confronts Zohk when two of his children are selected to be killed to feed serpents; Zohk releases the sons. Kavah then tears up the “register of blood,” leaves court, and rallies people to join the young Feridn, using his leather apron fixed on a javelin as a banner. After Kavah meets Feridn, the banner is adorned and becomes a sacred royal emblem honored by later kings. Feridn departs against Zohk, has Kavah forge an iron mace shaped like a cow’s head, prays at a shrine, and is taught magic secrets by a radiant personage who gives him a key. Feridn’s two brothers, jealous, attempt to kill him by rolling a rock down a mountain while he sleeps; he stops it using sorcery, and though aware of their plot, he forgives and elevates them.",
