  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Kandr, keeper of a talisman, reports to the tyrant Zohk that Feridn has released Zohk’s women, destroyed the talisman, seized the throne, and that Zohk’s magic has been dissolved by a higher power. Zohk’s army and people rebel against him, disgusted by his cruelty in feeding accursed serpents, and they support Feridn as new king. Zohk attempts a night attack on Feridn’s camp, but Feridn strikes him with a cow-headed mace. A supernatural voice tells Feridn not to kill Zohk yet, but to bind him in heavy chains and take him to a mountain cave to die lingeringly. The passage then praises Feridn’s justice and generosity as the source of his renown and claims he purified the world from sin and crime.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Kandr escapes and flees to Zohk, reporting the release of Zohk’s women, the destruction of the talisman, and the conquest of Zohk’s empire.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Kandr says three warriors have advanced upon Zohk’s kingdom, and one appears young and of the Kainian race.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Kandr says the young warrior seized the throne and that Zohk’s spells, sorceries, and magic were dissolved by a higher power; those in the palace (demon or man) were destroyed and their severed heads cast on the ground.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Zohk tries to appear cheerful before his army, suggesting the destruction of his palace may have been done by a playful guest; Kandr disputes this and mentions a cow-headed mace and Zohk’s secret chambers.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Kandr names the women Shahrnz and Arnawz as being brought to light from Zohk’s secret chambers.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Zohk rebukes Kandr for fleeing and says he will no longer share his confidence or bounty; Kandr replies that Zohk’s kingdom is overthrown and Zohk is lost.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "When soldiers and people learn of Feridn’s success, rebellion arises; they are horrified at Zohk’s cruelty in providing food for accursed serpents and they embrace the cause of the new king.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Zohk travels alone at night to Feridn’s camp intending to kill him, climbs a high place unobserved, and sees Feridn seated in soft dalliance with Shahrnz.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Zohk is described as consumed by the fire of jealousy and revenge.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Feridn is roused by a noise, rises, and strikes Zohk on the temples with a cow-headed mace, crushing the bone, and is about to strike again.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "A supernatural voice tells Feridn not to slay Zohk yet because his punishment must be prolonged; it instructs Feridn to bind Zohk with heavy chains and convey him to a mountain cave described as deep, dark, and horrible.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Feridn is said to perform the work of heaven and to have purified the world from sin and crime.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "The passage says Feridn was not an angel, and that by justice and generosity he gained his fame; it exhorts the exercise of these princely virtues to be renowned as Feridn.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    }
  ],
