    "summary": "Feridn arranges marriages for his three sons with three sisters from Yemen, then divides his empire among the sons. The two elder brothers (Slim and Tr) resent the allotment that gives Irij Persia, threaten war, and send an insulting message to Feridn. Feridn counsels contentment and peace, warns Irij of the danger, and advises him to avoid war by relinquishing dominion; Irij agrees and resolves to go to his brothers offering his kingdom to avert conflict.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Feridn has three sons named Slim, Tr, and Irij, and seeks three daughters from one father and mother for them to marry into a single family.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "A learned person named Chundel travels until he finds the King of Yemen (Sar) who has three daughters meeting the requested qualities; the sons marry them and receive dowries of treasure and jewels.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Feridn divides his empire: Slim receives Rm and Khwer; Tr receives Trn; Irij receives Irn (Persia).",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Slim complains to Tr that Irij received the most delightful and productive kingdom while they received wild, uncultivated regions; Tr agrees and they plan to deprive Irij of his dominions.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Slim dispatches a messenger to Feridn with unfilial language, demanding Irij be given a humbler portion or they will bring troops from Trn, Rm, and Chn against him and Persia.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Feridn responds with surprise and displeasure, says he gave them kingdoms, urges them to fear God, notes his life is nearing its end, and counsels peace and contentment instead of rebellion.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Feridn tells Irij the older brothers have confederated to seize his kingdom and put him to death; Feridn advises Irij cannot resist them and should seek peace by throwing away desire for dominion.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Irij agrees to sacrifice his throne and diadem rather than go to war with his brothers, reflecting on human transience and planning to go to them and place his kingdom at their disposal.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
