  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "A messenger reports Minchihr’s threatening reception and Feridun’s denunciations to the brothers Slim and Tr, who decide to strike quickly and march with a large army toward Irn. Feridun chooses to wait with patience, then Minchihr and Feridun’s forces deploy under appointed commanders, with the blacksmith’s sacred banner in front. Tr taunts Kabd about Minchihr’s royal equipment; Kabd condemns the brothers for murdering Irij and declares the cause righteous, while Minchihr says he seeks revenge and postpones battle for the day. The next day a bloody battle ends in Minchihr’s victory. Slim and Tr attempt a night attack, but Minchihr learns of it, sets an ambush, and kills Tr by throwing him from his horse and beheading him, sending the head to Feridun. Slim retreats into a fort; Minchihr pursues and besieges it, and when a warrior named Kak sallies out, Minchihr overpowers and kills him by seizing him and throwing him down.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
