      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Tr reproaches Kabd and questions who gave Minchihr armor and weapons; Kabd replies by accusing the brothers of murdering Irij and says the world will curse them until the day of doom; he claims those who die in the righteous cause will go to Heaven with sins forgotten.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Minchihr responds that strength and endurance are proven in battle, says he asks for revenge for Irij slain, and declares they will not fight that day; he then retires to a tent with wine and music.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "When morning comes, battle begins and many are slain; the plain is described as a sea of blood and the ground as slippery; Minchihr’s army is victorious and it is stated that Heaven is in his favor.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Slim and Tr plan a night attack; Minchihr’s spies discover it; Minchihr sets an ambush with thirty thousand men, confronts Tr, throws him from his saddle with a javelin, beheads him with a dagger, leaves the body for beasts, and sends the head as a trophy to Feridun.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Slim retreats to a fort; Minchihr besieges it; a warrior named Kak sallies out and throws a javelin that falls short; Minchihr seizes Kak by the girdle, lifts and throws him down, and Kak dies on the sand.",
