      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "In a second dream, Sam sees a beautiful young man leading an immense army with a banner and a Mobid at his left; a figure reproaches Sam for rejecting the boy because of silvery hair and says Heaven protected him.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Sam awakes terrified, weeps, and prays before the throne of the Almighty asking forgiveness and the restoration of his son.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "The Simurgh says it fed and protected Zal like a nurse, named him Dustan, taught him the language and cultivated his understanding, and must now restore him to Sam.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "The Simurgh gives Zal a feather and instructs him to put it on fire in difficulty or danger so the Simurgh will instantly appear to ensure his safety.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "The Simurgh conveys Zal to Sam and tells Sam to receive his son, who will be worthy of throne and diadem; Sam rejoices and says he will honor Zal in future.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "King Minchihr sends Nauder with a splendid istakbl to meet Sam and Zal; Zal kisses the earth before the king and receives a golden mace and helm.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
