    "summary": "An emissary accused of deception maintains a cover story. Rudabeh openly confesses her love for Zal and reports Sam's consent to the marriage. Rudabeh's father Mihrab reacts with rage and nearly attacks her but is restrained by Sindokht; he compares the union to angel and devil and invokes killing a snake. King Minchihr fears ruin from the union due to Mihrab's descent from Zahhak and seeks Sam's counsel. Sam recounts a victory over a demon-backed enemy and later, in a letter to Minchihr, highlights his service including slaying a vast dragon/monster whose poison and predation devastated the land, and he proposes yielding his station to Zal.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "An emissary is accused of treachery and of wearing male attire; she reveals nothing and claims to be a dealer in jewels and dresses showing merchandise to Rudabeh.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Sindokht goes to Rudabeh, and Rudabeh fearlessly acknowledges her devoted love for Zal, saying they have met and pledged mutual love.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Rudabeh says Sam has consented to the nuptials, partially satisfying her mother.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Mihrab, fearing the resentment of Sam and Minchihr, becomes enraged, draws a dagger, and would rush to destroy Rudabeh, but Sindokht restrains him by falling at his feet; Mihrab demands Rudabeh be brought before him after promising not to harm her.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Rudabeh refuses to remove her ornaments, appears before her father adorned with jewels and splendid apparel, and is received with surprise; Mihrab speaks of devil united to angel and says when a snake is met with in Arabia it is killed; Rudabeh says nothing and is permitted to retire with her mother.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Minchihr fears confusion and ruin to Persia from the united influence of Zal and Mihrab, citing that Feridun purified the world from Zahhak's abominations and that Mihrab is a descendant of Zahhak; Minchihr requires Sam to give advice.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Sam reports defeating an enemy monarch (descended on the mother's side from Zahhak) whose demon army was vast; Sam escapes a noose, shoots arrows, kills the opponent, and demons flee or become obedient to the Persian king.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Minchihr appoints Sam to a new enterprise: destroy Kabul by fire and sword, especially the house of Mihrab; Mihrab is called of the serpent-race, and he and his adherents are to be put to death; Sam tries to dissuade Minchihr without success.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Minchihr's intentions become known in Kabul and cause alarm; Zal returns to his father; Sam writes to deprecate Minchihr's wrath and sends Zal as messenger, recounting past services including destroying a prodigious dragon/monster.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "In Sam's letter, the monster's depredations are described (taking crocodile from stream and eagle from sky, leaving the country without inhabitants); Sam confronts it in God's name, shoots arrows (including through the tongue), and kills it with a battle-axe, after which the world regains peace; Sam says he is old and should resign his station to Zal.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    }
  ],
