      "text": "Brazen drums on elephants are sounded as the signal of departure as Afrsiyb’s army marches rapidly, overshadowing the earth.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Afrsiyb detaches thirty thousand troops under Shimass and Khazervn to Zabulistan to act against Zal, and writes to his father Poshang about his confidence and Sm’s death.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Brmn offers to challenge a Persian to single combat; Aghrras objects, but Afrsiyb orders Brmn to proceed.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Kobd, an aged Persian warrior and brother of Krun, accepts the single-combat challenge despite entreaties, stating that all are destined to die as ordained by the Creator.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "After an all-day duel, Brmn throws a stone that kills Kobd, who falls lifeless from his horse; Krun then brings forward the whole army to seek revenge.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Battle imagery includes dust clouds hiding the heavens and blood flowing like water; night ends the fighting.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Nauder, disappointed after repeated fighting, recalls Minchihr’s words and orders his sons Ts and Gustahem to return to Iran with his shubistan and take refuge on Mount Alberz so someone of Feridun’s race might survive approaching ruin.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "After a renewed battle, the Tartar host wins and many Persian chiefs fall, including Shahpr.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Afrsiyb dispatches Karkhn through the desert with horsemen to intercept and capture Nauder’s shubistan; Krun rides out at midnight without permission, fights Brmn, cuts off his head, hangs it on his saddle-bow, then attacks and defeats the Tartar troops and continues toward Iran.",
