  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Garshsp relies on Zal's counsel. Afrsiyb returns to his father Poshang, who condemns him for murdering his brother Aghrras and refuses to see him. Later, hearing Garshsp cannot rule Persia well, Poshang forgives Afrsiyb and sends him with a large army to invade Irn under a pretext of vengeance. Persian leaders appeal to Zal, who appoints his young son Rustem as commander, despite Rustem's youth. Zal trains Rustem, who takes up Sm's mace and seeks a powerful steed; he captures a promising foal called Rakush (said to be demon-descended), kills the foal's attacking dam, and finally subdues the foal. Rustem goes out with an army against Afrsiyb; Zal follows. Zal learns no other prince of Feridn's line is known, then discovers Kai-kobd living in obscurity on Mount Alberz, famed for wisdom and valor, and instructs Rustem to fetch him to take the throne.",
