  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "A Persian king recounts past wrongs that began with an ancestor's fratricide and continued with Afrsiyb's invasion and murders, yet proposes peace by yielding territory beyond the river Jihn and requiring Afrsiyb to swear an oath never to cross it. A messenger conveys the terms; the opposing army withdraws to the boundary; peace is concluded despite Rustem's objections. The king honors his champions, rules justly from Istakhar and later Irn for many years, and near death instructs his eldest son and appointed successor to rule with integrity, justice, and mercy.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "The speaker states the war began with Tr, who killed his brother Irij.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "The speaker says Afrsiyb crossed the river Jihn with a numerous force and invaded Persia, and that Nauder was murdered by Afrsiyb.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "The speaker says Afrsiyb stabbed his own brother, young Aghrras.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "The speaker offers peace by yielding the realm beyond the river Jihn and proposes the river as a boundary; Afrsiyb must take a solemn oath never to cross that limit or disturb the Persian throne again.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "A messenger conveys the intelligence to Poshang; the Trnian army withdraws within the prescribed line of division.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Rustem expostulates with the king against making peace; Kai-kobd prioritizes justice and tranquillity, and peace is concluded.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Kai-kobd confers the highest honors on Rustem and Zl, and other warriors receive bounty and gratitude.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Kai-kobd establishes his throne at Istakhar and governs with benevolence and clemency, giving equal consideration and justice; the strong have no power to oppress the weak.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "After ten years at Istakhar building towns and cities and improving the land, Kai-kobd removes his throne into Irn; his reign lasts one hundred years.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Kai-kobd has four sons; near death he enjoins the eldest (his successor) to follow integrity and justice and to be kind and merciful in administration.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
