  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Gw approaches the splendid city/region of Mzindern and reports its beauty and wealth to Kai-ks. The king of Mzindern summons the gigantic White Demon, who brings a night of unnatural darkness and hail that routs and destroys Kai-ks’s host; Kai-ks is left blind, his treasury taken, and his army killed or captured. Demon-warriors bind and starve the Iranian captives; Arzang seizes Kai-ks’s crown and jewels and escorts the blinded king and troops to Mzindern, then the White Demon returns home. Kai-ks secretly sends his condition to Zl, lamenting he ignored Zl’s counsel; Zl urges Rustem to arm and rescue the captive king. Zl describes two routes to Mzindern: a long one and a shorter, perilous one full of lions, demons, and sorcery; Rustem chooses the dangerous short way, trusts in God, arms himself, mounts his horse Rakush, and departs as his mother Rdbeh sorrowfully bids him farewell.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Gw comes near a city in Mzindern and finds it splendid, with streets crowded with adorned women; the treasure-chamber is full of gold and jewels, and the country has abundant cattle.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Information about the discovery is sent to Kai-ks, who delights in Mzindern as a blessed region and a \"garden of beauty.\"",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "The king of Mzindern, grieved and alarmed by the invasion, calls the gigantic White Demon for aid.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Kai-ks encamps near the city and prepares to overthrow the enemy, but at night a cloud and deep darkness cover the earth and tremendous hail-stones fall on the Persian host, causing destruction and scattering survivors.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "When morning comes, Kai-ks has no light to his eyes; his treasury is captured and his soldiers are killed or made prisoners.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Kai-ks laments that he did not follow the wise counsel of Zl and remains afflicted for seven days; on the eighth day he hears the White Demon speak, mocking his attempt to conquer Mzindern.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Twelve thousand demon-warriors are selected to guard Iranian captives; chiefs and soldiers are bound and given only enough food to keep them alive.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Arzang, a demon-leader, takes Kai-ks’s wealth, crown, and jewels and escorts the captive king and troops—deprived of sight—to Mzindern, delivering them to that country’s monarch; the White Demon then returns to his abode.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Kai-ks, though guarded, sends an account of his blind and helpless condition to Zl, urgently asking for rescue; Zl reacts with vexation and speaks privately with Rustem.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Zl tells Rustem to arm and ride Rakush to free Kai-ks, explaining he is too old for war; Rustem notes the long journey and Zl describes two roads: a tedious one and a shorter one full of danger, lions, demons, and sorcery that could reach Mzindern in seven days.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Rustem chooses the short dangerous road, says he will trust in God for victory, arms himself under Heaven’s protection, and departs from Sstn with his horse Rakush; his mother Rdbeh takes leave of him with great sorrow.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    }
