  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "They contrived to rob an eagle's nest of its young... in the middle Ks was seated in great pomp with a goblet of wine before him... they ascended higher and higher in the clouds... their strength failed them... the whole fabric came tumbling down from the sky.",
    "summary": "Kai-Kaus is freed and restored to the Persian throne by Rustem. After defeating Afrasiyab and securing the kingdom, Kai-Kaus orders demons to build splendid palaces on Mount Alberz. Iblis exploits the king's vanity by having a disguised demon flatter him and stress that he cannot fly, prompting Kai-Kaus to seek ascent to the heavens. His astrologers steal and rear young eagles, bind four eagles to a wooden framework baited with goat flesh on javelins, and seat the king on it; the hungry eagles lift the contraption into the clouds. Exhausted, the eagles fail and the structure crashes into a desolate area in Chin, leaving Kai-Kaus hungry and despairing until demons sent by his ministers find him.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "quoted"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Kai-Kaus and his heroes are released from fetters and removed from a mountain-fortress; Rustem reseats Kai-Kaus on his throne and gathers valuables for the public treasury.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Kai-Kaus musters a very large army from allied troops and sends Afrasiyab a message commanding him to quit Iran and be content with Turan.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Afrasiyab promises his daughter in marriage and a kingdom to whoever takes Rustem alive.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "In battle, many of Afrasiyab's chiefs fall; Afrasiyab fights Rustem, then escapes and flees back to Turan, leaving Kai-Kaus in possession of the kingdom.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Kai-Kaus resumes rule with justice and liberality, assigns warriors to secure several states, and grants Rustem the title 'Jahani Pahlavan' (Champion of the World).",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Kai-Kaus directs demons to construct two splendid palaces and separate mansions on Mount Alberz, decorated lavishly with gold, silver, and precious stones.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Iblis observes the king's vanity and persuades demons to assist; one demon disguises as a domestic servant and presents a nosegay while flattering the king and stating that he cannot fly.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Kai-Kaus becomes concerned with ascending the heavens without wings and consults astrologers, who propose a method.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Astrologers steal young eagles from a nest, rear them, build an aloes-wood framework with four javelins baited with goat flesh, bind one eagle at each corner, and seat Kai-Kaus in the middle with a goblet of wine.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "The hungry eagles fly upward toward the bait, lifting the throne/structure into the clouds and carrying the king far beyond his country; later they weaken, and the structure tumbles down and crashes in a desolate place in Chin.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Kai-Kaus is left alone, hungry and despairing, until discovered by a band of demons sent by his ministers to search for him.",
