  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Rustem and allied warriors learn that King Kai-Kaus (Ks) has fallen into trouble; they go to him, rebuke him for folly and impiety, and he returns to his palace, repenting in seclusion for forty days before resuming just rule. Later Rustem holds a seven-day feast; the group decides on a feigned hunting expedition into Afrasiyab’s sporting grounds. Afrasiyab attempts to trap and capture Rustem and the seven champions by blocking routes with a large army. Battle follows; Rustem and his companions rout the Turanians, killing notable opponents. Rustem pursues Afrasiyab, briefly snares him with a noose, but Afrasiyab escapes and retreats across a boundary stream, leaving many dead behind.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Rustem, Gudarz (Gdarz), and Tus (Ts) hear what has happened to King Ks and set off to assist him.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Gudarz criticizes Ks as lacking reason and says Ks is being punished for attempting to discover the secrets of the Heavens; he exhorts Ks to be obedient to God.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Ks weeps, acknowledges folly, returns to his palace, and remains unseen for forty days in shame and repentance; afterward he resumes governing with liberality, clemency, and justice.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Rustem holds a splendid feast for seven days; on the eighth day they prepare to march, sending an advance party to reconnoitre the enemy.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "The group decides on a pretended hunting party to go to the sporting grounds of Afrasiyab.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Afrasiyab learns of the movement and hopes to get Rustem and his seven champions into his thrall; he assembles thirty thousand veterans to occupy positions and avenues near the sporting grounds.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Rustem declares he would not fear the king of Turan even alone with his horse Rakush and weapons; he challenges Afrasiyab to cross the boundary-river.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "A cup-bearer produces goblets of red wine; Rustem pledges his royal master, and others join in a demonstration of attachment to the king.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
