    "summary": "The governor of a fort reports to his monarch that the young warrior Sohrab has defeated Hujr and is besieging the walls; he urges that only Rustem can save the country. A messenger carries the warning, while the fort’s defenders escape at night, leaving the fortress empty. At dawn Sohrab assaults the gates, finds the place deserted, and laments the loss of a warrior-maid he desires. A Turanian chief reproaches him for weeping over love and urges pursuit of conquest. Sohrab’s ambition revives and he declares Afrasiyab will rule Persia. Meanwhile Kai-Kaus learns of the invasion, gathers his chiefs at an ivory throne, and they agree to summon Rustem from rural rest.",
