  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "A hunting party meets a beautiful young woman in the forest near the river Jihun; she says she fled an angry father who sought to marry her to Poshang of Turan. Two men in the party quarrel over her, but the king takes her for himself; she bears a son, Saiwush, whose promise is foretold by astrologers. The hero Rustem raises and trains Saiwush in Zabulistan before bringing him back to court. Later, Sudaveh, daughter of the Shah of Hamavaran, falls in love with Saiwush and secretly summons him, but he refuses to dishonor his father’s court.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "At cockcrow, Ts goes hunting with Gw, Gdarz, and horsemen near the banks of the Jihun; in the forest they encounter a very beautiful damsel alone.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "The damsel says her father is violent; she left home to escape him, crossed the river Jihun, and has been in the forest for three days because her horse could not carry her farther.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "She identifies her father as Shwer of the race of Feridn; she refused many suitors, including a proposed marriage to Poshang, ruler of Trn, due to his ugliness and bad temper.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Ts and Gw both fall in love with the damsel and quarrel; they agree to refer the decision to the king.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "When the king sees the damsel, he takes her for himself after confirming her distinguished family connections.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "A son is born to the king and the woman; astrologers calculate he is of wonderful promise and he is named Saiwush.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Ks seeks to develop Saiwush’s talents and is gratified when Rustem agrees to take him to Zbulistn for instruction suitable to his rank.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Saiwush is taught horsemanship, archery, courtly conduct, hunting with falcon and leopard, and the manners and duties of kings; he later returns with Rustem to the royal court and is received with distinction.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Preceptors continue to teach Saiwush for seven more years, after which he is freed from study.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Sdveh, daughter of the Shh of Hmvern, sees Saiwush with his father, falls in love, summons him to a secret bower, and Saiwush refuses because he will not shame his father’s hall.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
