  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Gerswaz, Afrsiyb’s brother, bears jealousy toward Saiwush and reports to Afrsiyb that Saiwush is ambitious and preparing rebellion. Afrsiyb hesitates to believe the accusation but considers sending Saiwush back to his father Kai-ks. Gerswaz proposes an artifice: summon Saiwush with a friendly letter and then seize him. Saiwush initially responds with prompt obedience, but Gerswaz privately urges delay and pride; Saiwush is persuaded to postpone his departure, using Ferangs’s feigned illness as a reason. Gerswaz carries the delayed reply to Afrsiyb, and Afrsiyb interprets the delay as proof of treachery, assembles an army under Gerswaz, and moves against Saiwush. Ferangs advises Saiwush to flee by a circuitous route back to Iran; she cannot accompany him. Saiwush departs with three hundred Iranians and asks Ferangs to name their child Kai-khosru if she bears a son.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
