  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Saiwush is pursued, captured, and brought to Afrsiyb. Ferangs pleads for his life but Afrsiyb orders his execution, insisting his blood not stain the earth. Saiwush prays for a son to vindicate him and avenge the murder. After beheading, some blood spills; a tree grows from the spot and is later believed to have virtues. A tempest and darkness accompany the death. Afrsiyb then orders Ferangs secretly killed to prevent any issue from the marriage, but Prn intervenes and takes her into his care, with instructions to bring the child to Afrsiyb when born.",
