  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Afrsiyb learns his realm has been devastated and calls his warriors to vengeance. Rustem, avenging Saiwush, also seeks the hidden prince Kai-khosru. Gdarz dreams of the prince’s location and that Gw alone can restore him. Gw undertakes a harsh journey, using and then killing guides to prevent discovery, and finds a youth by a fountain; they recognize each other, and Gw confirms the prince’s royal lineage by a hereditary bodily mark. Gw escorts Kai-khosru and his mother Ferangs toward Irn; Ferangs directs Gw to seize Afrsiyb’s horses (including Behzd, once Saiwush’s). Afrsiyb sends Kulbd with three hundred horsemen in pursuit; Gw, trusting a prophecy that Kai-khosru will be king of kings, attacks and routs them, then the travelers continue through wilderness toward Irn.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Afrsiyb hears of the plundering and burning of his land and urges his warriors to seek vengeance, condemning anyone unmoved by the nation’s suffering.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Rustem sends to remote parts of Tartary to search for Kai-khosru.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Gdarz has a dream in which the young prince reveals his residence and says Gw is destined to restore him to his birth-right.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Gw travels toward the boundary of Chn, taking successive guides and then killing them to prevent discovery; he endures sleeplessness and privation, living on wild ass flesh and skin.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Gw meets people searching for Kai-ks on Prn-wsah’s orders, conceals his purpose, and later discovers a youth sitting by a fountain holding a cup; each identifies the other by name and lineage.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Gw confirms the youth’s royal lineage when the youth removes his garments and Gw sees a hereditary mark associated with the race of Kai-kobd.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Ferangs urges immediate departure and points to a meadow where Afrsiyb’s horses can be found; Gw captures Behzd (formerly Saiwush’s) and another horse with a kamund.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Afrsiyb dispatches Kulbd with three hundred horsemen; Gw arms himself, mounts Behzd, attacks, and routs the pursuers, acting confidently because of a prophecy about Kai-khosru’s future kingship.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "After the victory, Kai-khosru is disappointed he was not awakened; Gw says he did not wish to disturb him and credits the prince’s good fortune for the triumph; the three continue through wilderness.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    }
