  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Prn (a commander) pursues fugitives after Kulbd’s defeat and confronts Gw, who insists on fighting alone to protect the young Kai-khosru, said to be destined for kingship. Gw captures Prn with a kamund and brings him before Kai-khosru. Ferangs pleads for Prn’s life due to past help, but Gw cites an oath to shed Prn’s blood. Kai-khosru proposes a loophole: pierce Prn’s ear-lobes and let blood fall to the ground to satisfy the oath; Prn is then released instead of being sent to Ks for execution.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
