  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Zal and Rustem hear of Khosru's accession, go to court with gifts, and pay homage; Khosru asks Rustem to help take vengeance for Saiwush's death, and Rustem agrees.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "A royal banquet is held; it is agreed to march a large army against Afrasiyab; Zal asks to remain in his province due to age.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Khosru speaks of finding no happiness or restful sleep until he is avenged on the \"tyrant of Turan\" to please the spirit of his butchered father.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Ks delivers the imperial army to Khosru and explains the character and merits of important individuals; multiple commanders and groupings are appointed across the army (right, left, centre, and a separate guard).",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "On the march, Khosru tells Frburz and Ts that his brother Ferd has built a strong fort (Kullb) in Bokhra and lives there with his mother Glshaher; Khosru orders them not to molest Ferd and to pass around his possessions.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Frburz avoids Ferd's territory, but Ts chooses to go through the cultivated country and approaches Ferd's fort; Ferd assumes Ts comes to fight and prepares to oppose him; Ts sends his son-in-law R to explain peaceful intent, but Ferd rejects this and kills R in the ensuing conflict.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "After R is killed, Ts draws up his army and besieges Ferd's fort; Ferd sallies out and attacks with bow and arrows, killing Ts's horse and throwing Ts to the ground; Gw rushes forward to capture Ts but is likewise unhorsed.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Byzun, Gw's son, attempts revenge; Ferd kills Byzun's horse and unseats him; Byzun rises and challenges Ferd to single combat; they fight with spears briefly; Ferd retreats into the fort and from its walls throws stones, wounding Byzun so he withdraws.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Ts vows that on the following day no man will remain alive in the fort.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Ferd's mother dreams the fortress has taken fire and all inhabitants have been consumed to death; she tells Ferd, and Ferd replies that he does not dread death, that no one is immortal, that he seeks a spotless name in war, and that their lot is written and protected by divine power.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7",
        "ev:8"
      ]
    }
  ],
