    "summary": "Rustem kills Ushkabs in single combat with bow and arrows, astonishing the opposing host. The enemy takes Ushkabs's body to the Khakn of Chin, who inspects the deeply-penetrating arrow. The next day Kms challenges Rustem; Alwund (Rustem’s pupil) is slain, then Rustem defeats Kms using a kamund (lasso/rope), captures him, and Kms is put to death. Chingush also challenges Rustem, flees, is pursued, pulled from his saddle by the horse’s tail, and killed; his body is left to vultures. When no one else answers Rustem’s challenge, Hmn comes to remonstrate and seek an end to the war, but Rustem cites Afrasiyab’s crimes, especially the murder of Saiwush, as unforgivable. Rustem refuses to reveal his name and asks to speak privately with Prn-wsah, while the enemy fears devastation if this warrior is indeed Rustem.",
