  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "A peasant reports to King Kai-khosru a wild-ass-like apparition attacking the royal horses. Rustem is summoned to deal with it. The creature repeatedly vanishes when Rustem tries to catch or strike it, and Rustem identifies it as the demon Akwn Dw. When Rustem sleeps near a spring, Akwn Dw lifts up the ground and Rustem together and offers to throw him into the sea or abandon him on a mountain. Rustem, relying on the demon’s contrarian nature, asks to be left on the mountain; Akwn Dw instead throws him into the ocean. Rustem kills attacking crocodiles, swims ashore, thanks Heaven, recovers his horse Rakush from Afrsiyb’s herd, and drives off the herd. Afrsiyb attacks but is forced to flee, and Rustem delivers the seized horses (and four elephants) to Kai-khosru, then returns toward Akwn Dw’s vicinity and meets the demon again.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Kai-khosru sits in a garden with warriors, feasting with music, when a peasant reports a mysterious wild ass that has rushed among the horses in the royal stables and caused injury, seeming like an evil spirit.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Rustem is requested and goes searching; on the fourth day he encounters the wild ass and tries to capture it alive with a kamund, but it vanishes.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Rustem concludes the being is Akwn Dw; repeated attempts with sword, spear, and arrow fail because the animal vanishes, and he continues for three days and nights fighting \"against a shadow.\"",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Rustem rests near a green spot by a limpid fountain or rivulet of spring water; he lets Rakush graze and falls asleep.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Akwn Dw rushes in, digs up the ground around Rustem, lifts the plot of ground and Rustem together, places them on his head, and carries them away.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Akwn Dw asks whether to plunge Rustem into the sea or leave him on a dreary mountain without succor; Rustem answers requesting not to be plunged into the sea but to be cast on the mountain, stating sea means nothing escapes.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Akwn Dw acts to thwart Rustem’s expressed desire and throws him headlong into the deep ocean.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "In the ocean, a crocodile attacks Rustem; he draws his sword and cuts off its head, kills another similarly, and the water is crimsoned with blood; he then swims safely to shore and thanks Heaven for protection.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Rustem returns to the fountain where he left Rakush but finds the horse missing; he later finds Rakush among Afrsiyb’s herd of horses, catches him, and decides to capture and drive away the whole herd to Kai-khosru.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Afrsiyb’s horse-keepers pursue Rustem; Rustem declares his identity and lineage and past conquest of Afrsiyb, and the keepers flee.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Afrsiyb arrives at the horse meadows, learns Rustem has carried off the herd, attacks with troops, but is compelled to flee; Rustem’s seizure includes the herd and four elephants, which go to Kai-khosru.",
