  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Akwn Dw taunts Rustem, who ensnares the demon with his kamund and decapitates him, sending the severed head as a trophy to King Kai-khosru. Rustem is honored at court and then returns toward Zbulistn. The narrative then shifts to Armenians petitioning Kai-khosru for relief from destructive wild boars. Byzun volunteers to exterminate them; despite Gw's objection due to his youth, the king allows it on condition that the veteran Girgn accompany him. Byzun and Girgn hunt and kill many boars; Byzun burns the forest and cultivation to deny the animals sustenance, and prepares boar heads and tusks as proof to send to Kai-khosru. Girgn grows envious and manipulates Byzun while he is warmed with wine, praising him and enticing him with a tale of a nearby garden of perpetual spring visited by Manjeh, daughter of Afrsiyb. They go there; Manjeh sees Byzun, falls in love, and sends her nurse to learn who he is and where he comes from.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Akwn Dw speaks a taunt challenging Rustem, suggesting he has escaped death and seeks to fight again.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Rustem throws his kamund, entangles Akwn Dw, then strikes with his sword and severs the demon's head from its body.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Rustem sends the severed head of the monster as a trophy to Kai-khosru; the king regards it with amazement because of its hideous expression and vast size.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Rustem pays his respects to Kai-khosru, is received with honor and affection, enjoys hospitality at court, then returns to Zbulistn, accompanied partway by Kai-khosru and warriors.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "The people of Armn petition Kai-khosru for protection because herds of wild boars overrun their country, destroying fields and orchards and making it dangerous to go abroad.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Kai-khosru is described as feasting with warriors at a banquet, drinking wine, listening to music and songs of damsels, when he receives the complaint.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Kai-khosru refers the grievance to counsellors and nobles for an immediate remedy; Byzun offers to undertake exterminating the boars; Gw objects that Byzun is too young; the king permits Byzun to go if accompanied by the veteran Girgn.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Byzun and Girgn travel several days to a place between Irn and Trn; many boars are hunted and killed; Byzun sets fire to the forest and reduces cultivation to ashes to destroy the boars' sustenance.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Byzun cuts off the heads of the boars and removes their tusks to send to Kai-khosru as proof; Girgn becomes envious and tries to prevent the trophies being sent, then plots to remove Byzun by manipulating him while he is warm with wine and praising him.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Girgn describes a nearby beautiful garden of perpetual spring visited in the vernal season by Manjeh, daughter of Afrsiyb, and suggests they could encamp there and secure virgins for the king.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Byzun and Girgn go to the princess's retreat; Manjeh sees Byzun from her summer-tent, becomes enamoured, and sends her nurse to inquire about him and his origin.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:11"
      ]
    }
  ],
