  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "After being defeated, Afrsiyb encounters a huge stranger named Barz, who claims not to know his father and says his birth is mysterious. Afrsiyb promises Barz marriage to his daughter and rule over Chin and Machin if Barz destroys Rustem, Afrsiyb’s invincible enemy. Barz boasts he can defeat Rustem. Barz’s mother warns that the rich gifts he has received will be his shroud and urges him to avoid Rustem, who has defeated demons and great warriors. Barz rejects her counsel, asserting his superior strength and that life is in God’s hands. Afrsiyb assigns masters to train Barz in weapons and wrestling; Barz quickly proves strong in drills and is described by onlookers as seeming non-human, like the Evil One, and like Mount Alberz in armor. Barz urges immediate action against Rustem and King Kai-khosru; Afrsiyb gives him ten thousand horsemen and appoints Hmn and Brmn to accompany him.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Afrsiyb, traveling in despair after a defeat, meets a man of huge and terrifying stature on the road toward Chin and Machin.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "The stranger says he is a villager, does not know his father, and that his mother never mentioned his father’s name; he says his birth is \"wrapped in mystery.\"",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Afrsiyb describes Rustem as an invincible enemy whom weapons do not affect and likens him to a mountain of steel; Barz boasts he can reduce many such mountains to dust.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Afrsiyb promises Barz his daughter in marriage and the monarchy of Chin and Machin if Barz destroys Rustem.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Afrsiyb gives Barz costly presents (gold, jewels, horses, elephants), and Barz becomes proud and dazzled by them.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Barz’s mother warns that the presents will be his winding-sheet and that Rustem has conquered demons and overthrown Afrsiyb’s best warriors; she urges caution.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Barz rejects his mother’s warning, says life is in the hands of the Almighty, and claims his strength is superior to Rustem’s; Afrsiyb appoints two masters to train him in weapons and wrestling/noose-throwing.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "After ten days of training, Barz can overthrow eighteen warriors at one time; observers say he does not seem of human birth, has the aspect of the Evil One, and looks like Alberz mountain clad in mail.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Barz urges immediate advance to meet Rustem and King Kai-khosru, boasting he will take their heads and bring the Persian crown and throne as trophies; Afrsiyb assigns him ten thousand horsemen and appoints Hmn and Brmn to accompany him.",
