  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Kai-khosru sends troops against Afrsiyb’s renewed invasion; Ts and Frburz are defeated by Barz, captured, and threatened with death. Rustem and Gustahem infiltrate the enemy camp at night, kill a watchman, and rescue the chained prisoners. Afrsiyb dispatches Barz to challenge Rustem; Barz and Rustem fight with bow, maces, and wrestling, and Rustem is badly wounded but hides it. They agree to resume the combat the next day. Rustem asks to call his son Fermurz (absent in Hindustan) and later seeks to travel to Sistan to obtain a remedy from the Smrgh; he prays through the night, and near morning Fermurz arrives.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Kai-khosru orders Ts and Frburz to oppose Afrsiyb’s invasion with twelve thousand horsemen, and then marches after them with a larger army.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Ts meets the enemy; a battle lasts a whole day and night; Barz is victorious; Persian warriors flee; Ts and Frburz are taken prisoner, bound, and placed in Hmn’s charge.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "In Afrsiyb’s pavilion, Afrsiyb sits on a throne with Barz at his right and Prn-wsah at his left; Ts and Frburz stand in chains before them.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Afrasiyb tells the captives they will be put to death the next day in the manner he slew Saiwush.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Rustem and Gustahem wait until a watchman is off guard; they kill him and carry the prisoners away, knock off their chains, and conduct them back to Kai-khosru.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Afrasiyb is told a Persian champion killed the watchman and carried off the prisoners; Prn says it must be Rustem; Afrsiyb sends his army to challenge Rustem to single combat.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "In the challenge exchange, Barz says that if Rustem is fire, Barz is water and can quench Rustem’s flames.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Rustem and Barz fight first with bows and arrows, then with maces until the maces bend, then by wrestling with wrenches and grasps.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Barz strikes Rustem a severe blow on the head; Rustem’s arm is disabled; Rustem conceals the effects of the wound and proposes finishing the combat the following day; Barz agrees and they part.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6",
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Barz reports to Afrsiyb that Rustem and Rustem’s horse seemed as hard as flint and that Barz’s blows were without effect.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Rustem shows his wounded arm to Khosru, says his son Fermurz is fighting in Hindustan, and asks to call him; Khosru says he will fight Barz himself, but Gdarz objects and says other chiefs should encounter Barz first.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Rustem tells his brother Zra to prepare a litter so he can go to Sistan to obtain a remedy from the Smrgh; pain keeps him awake and he prays to the Supreme Being; near morning Zra reports Fermurz’s arrival and Rustem asks him to rest, then Rustem sleeps.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    }
  ],
