  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Afrsiyb challenges Kai-khosru to single combat as a way to avoid wider bloodshed, invoking God as the judge of victory. Kai-khosru prepares to accept, but Rustem and Barz restrain him; Barz threatens self-harm to prevent the king from fighting. Barz then rides out and duels Afrsiyb, who wounds him with an arrow; the fight expands into a general battle after Hmn and Prn urge Afrsiyb not to risk himself. Barz is surrounded and badly wounded, but Rustem, Fermurz, and then Kai-khosru arrive with support; the Trnians flee and Afrsiyb escapes. Rustem, claiming great age, asks leave to return home, and Kai-khosru rewards his warriors and returns to his capital while Zl and Rustem go to Sstn.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
