  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Kai-khosru sends Gdarz with allies and a large army to renew war against Afrsiyb in Trn. Battles occur in which Hmn and later Prn are killed. Afrsiyb laments Prn's death. Kai-khosru advances across the Jihn and requests Rustem's counsel for the young commander Lohursp. Afrsiyb digs up hidden treasure to raise forces and sends his son Shydah-Poshang as ambassador offering peace secured by hostage and promises, or else proposing single combat to decide the war. Kai-khosru refuses peace until avenging Saiwush, and his warriors warn that Afrsiyb's proposal is deceitful and connected with fraud and sorcery.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Kai-khosru commissions Gdarz to lead a new expedition against Afrsiyb in Trn, stating Rustem has already served in repeated campaigns.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Gdarz travels toward Trn with Gw, Ts, Byzun, and a large army; Fermurz is ordered to invade Hindstn and then march toward the borders of Chn and M-chn to cooperate with Gdarz and capture Afrsiyb.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "In Trn, Hmn is appointed with a large force to resist Gdarz, and a reserve army is assembled under Prn.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Gdarz orders Byzun to attack Hmn; in their battle Hmn is killed, and his defeated troops retreat to join Prn's forces.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Gdarz reports the enemy's strengthened position to Kai-khosru; Kai-khosru sends reinforcements and writes to Sstn requesting aid from Rustem.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "The war continues for two years with continual recruitment, until a great battle in which Prn is killed and nearly his entire army is destroyed; the victory occurs without Rustem, who remains in Sstn.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Afrsiyb grieves Prn's death, describing Prn as refuge, friend, brother, counselor, and guide, and vows not to rest until vengeance is inflicted on the foe.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "After hearing of Prn's death, Kai-khosru marches quickly, crosses the Jihn, and passes through Samerknd and Bokhra to meet the Trnians.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Afrsiyb has hidden treasure dug up to assemble a large army, appointing his son Shydah-Poshang over one hundred thousand horsemen; Kai-khosru appoints Lohursp with eight thousand horsemen and asks Rustem to counsel Lohursp due to his youth and inexperience.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Afrsiyb increases Shydah's force and sends Shydah as ambassador proposing peace, offering one son as hostage, troops for service, and a promise not to break engagements; if peace is refused, Afrsiyb proposes single combat between himself and Kai-khosru, or between Shydah and Kai-khosru, with surrender of Trn if Shydah is killed.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Kai-khosru regards Afrsiyb's proposal as weakness and refuses to make peace until he has inflicted on Afrsiyb the death that Saiwush suffered.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Kai-khosru hosts Shydah respectfully, then consults his warriors; he remarks on Shydah's fierce appearance and orders his mail prepared, but Rustem and others insist the duel must not be allowed and describe Afrsiyb as fraudulent, deceitful, and associated with sorcery.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    }
