    "summary": "Rustem advises Kai-khosru not to risk fighting Shydah; nevertheless Shydah insists on combat. Kai-khosru writes to Afrsiyb rejecting peace, demanding surrender, and asserting that strength and victory come from God/Heaven. Kai-khosru sends Shydah a message predicting his doom and his father's grief. Kai-khosru and Shydah wrestle; Kai-khosru overpowers and kills Shydah with a dagger, then orders the body washed with musk and rose-water and buried with a tomb. Afrsiyb, grieving, refuses to answer the envoy Krun and marches to war; a furious battle ends with Turanian defeat and Afrsiyb is forced to flee. Kai-khosru pursues to the borders of Chin; the Khakn offers gifts but, threatened, withdraws protection, forcing Afrsiyb to seek refuge elsewhere.",
