  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Kai-khosru becomes devoted to a religious life, relinquishes rule, and insists he must prepare for departure to the next world after receiving a mysterious warning. Despite pleas from nobles and the arrival of Zal and Rustem, he remains resolved. He then holds a seven-day feast, gives wealth to the poor, assigns lands and offices to leading figures, appoints Lohursp as successor, and begins a journey toward a fountain he has seen in a dream where he expects to die.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Kai-khosru abandons the duties of sovereignty and commits state affairs to ministers, stating his affection is not for the transitory world.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Chiefs and warriors remonstrate; the nobles ask Zal and Rustem to try to change the king’s disposition, and some attribute his change to Iblis and an “evil eye.”",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "In conversation with Zal and Rustem, the king says he is weary of life’s troubles and cannot endure mankind’s deceptions and perfidy.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "The king reports that a mysterious voice warned him that the time of his departure is near and told him to prepare the load for his journey and not neglect his warning angel.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Kai-khosru says he must seek a solitary cell and there resign his soul to heaven.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "He orders tents pitched in the desert, opens his treasury, holds a seven-day feast, and distributes food and money to indigent people, widows, and orphans until want is removed throughout the empire.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "He appoints Lohursp as successor and directs the people to pay allegiance to him; he also assigns offices and regions to multiple named warriors and officials.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Kai-khosru says a fountain has been pointed out to him in dreams, and that when he visits it his life will be resigned to its Creator; he then sets out and takes leave of Zal and Rustem.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Zal and Rustem lament that he seeks the tomb, and they say no mortal previously trod the supernal way and living saw the face of God.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    }
  ],
