  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Lohursp abdicates and lives as a recluse near Balkh. The narrative contrasts earlier rulers' worship of God with later idolatry. Gushtsp, a great king, favors the learned Zerdusht, who teaches doctrines of fire-worship and performs marvels, including producing a tree whose leaves and fruit grant knowledge and wisdom. Zerdusht heals the dying Lohursp, claims prophetic authority and journeys to heaven and hell, and says a sacred book (Zendavesta) descended to him. Gushtsp becomes his disciple and adopts fire-worship. Zerdusht urges Gushtsp to stop paying tribute to Arjsp of Chin; letters are exchanged, Arjsp threatens war and sends a message via demons; Gushtsp’s council opts for war and hostilities begin.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Lohursp relinquishes imperial authority, adopts a recluse’s coarse habit, retires to a pilgrimage place near Balkh, and lives in a solitary cell devoted to prayer and worship.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "A statement asserts earlier sovereigns worshipped God who granted crowns, but later times produced idolatry and pagan faith.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Gushtsp and his wife Kitabn have two sons (Isfendiyr and Bashtan) described as pious and devoted to the Almighty.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Minor sovereigns pay Gushtsp tribute, except Arjsp (ruler of Chin and Machin), whose army consists of Dws, Peris, and men; Gushtsp sends him a yearly tributary present.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Zerdusht, described as accomplished in divine knowledge, meets Gushtsp, gains his confidence, and explains doctrines of fire-worshippers.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Zerdusht causes a tree to appear before Gushtsp’s house; eating its leaves makes one learned in mysteries of the future world, and eating its fruit makes one perfect in wisdom and holiness.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Zerdusht goes to Balkh to relieve Lohursp’s near-fatal illness and restores him to health; afterward Gushtsp becomes Zerdusht’s disciple.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Zerdusht claims to be God’s prophet; says he has been to heaven and hell; claims he can send people to heaven by prayer and send those he is angry with to hell; describes seven celestial mansions and sapphire thrones and knowledge from an attendant angel.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Zerdusht says the sacred book Zendavesta descended from above for him and promises Gushtsp celestial felicity if he follows it; Gushtsp converts and adopts fire-worship.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Zerdusht says he prepared a ladder and ascended into heaven to see the Almighty.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Zerdusht reproaches Gushtsp for paying tribute to Arjsp; Gushtsp sends a dispatch refusing future tribute and asserting power to resist.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Arjsp replies accusing Gushtsp of abandoning the right path, calls Zerdusht a seducer with magician-like arts and Iblis-like attributes, threatens invasion with fire and sword, and sends the letter by two demon messengers familiar with sorcery.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "Gushtsp convenes a council; Jamsp urges prudence, while Zerdusht urges war; Isfendiyr offers to lead but Zarr objects due to his youth and proposes to command; Gushtsp agrees and sends a threatening reply.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "The exchange of menaces leads to immediate prosecution of war, and Arjsp hastens into Iran.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:14"
      ]
    }
