    "summary": "Gushtsp visits Zal and Rustem to convert them to Zerdusht’s religion; Rustem accepts the Zendavesta and adopts the faith (said to be from fear). Meanwhile Isfendiyr remains imprisoned; Bahman laments. Arjsp sends Kahram to attack unprotected Balkh; Lohursp is forced from religious retirement to lead a small force and is slain. Kahram occupies Balkh, imprisons the people, destroys Guber places of worship, kills the altar-keeper, and burns the Zendavesta. A woman escapes to warn Gushtsp, who hurries back; a battle follows and Gushtsp is defeated and takes refuge in a mountain-fort. He consults Jamsp, who foretells recovery only through Isfendiyr. Gushtsp sends a letter asking pardon and promising to restore the crown and punish enemies; Gurzam is chained. Jamsp persuades Isfendiyr to help; a blacksmith removes his chains (causing him to faint), and Isfendiyr reconciles with Gushtsp. Gushtsp restores him to command and executes Gurzam before the prince.",
