      "text": "The passage explicitly frames Isfendiyr’s upcoming deeds as “seven great labours,” following mention of Rustem’s seven labours.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Isfendiyr promises Kurugsar a principality if Isfendiyr conquers Arjsp’s kingdom and restores his sisters to liberty, and warns that treachery or falsehood will be punished by death.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Kurugsar describes three routes to the brazen fortress: a three-month pleasant route, a two-month less agreeable route, and a seven-day route called the Heft-khan with a monster or severe difficulty at every stage; he says no monarch has yet ventured it and that an attempted party will be lost.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "The Heft-khan route is described as beset with wolves and dragons and an enchantress armed with spells, with harmful beings and obstacles appearing at every step.",
