  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Isfendiyr undertakes successive stages of a perilous journey (labors). In the fifth stage he uses an armed, horse-drawn vehicle as a trap to wound and kill the giant Smrgh; its young flee. His guide Kurugsar warns of an impending deadly snowstorm and urges retreat, but Isfendiyr refuses and the troops ultimately reaffirm loyalty. In the sixth stage a severe snow-and-wind storm forces the party to shelter in mountain caves for three days without food; they pray to the Almighty and the storm ceases. Kurugsar then describes the next route to the Brazen Fortress (Arjsp’s residence): a belt of burning sand like fire with no water, and a fortress with no visible path and said to be militarily unreducible.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Isfendiyr travels with a small army across desert, plain, mountain, and wilderness to the neighborhood of the Smrgh.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Isfendiyr prepares an immense horse-drawn vehicle (a machine) equipped with swords and spears as a stratagem.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "The Smrgh descends from the mountain and tries to seize the vehicle with claws and then beak; both are injured and the Smrgh weakens from loss of blood.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Isfendiyr springs out of the carriage and kills the Smrgh with a sword, dividing it into two parts; the Smrgh's young flee after witnessing the parent's death.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Bashtan and the army arrive and are amazed at the Smrgh's size and its defeat; Kurugsar turns pale with astonishment and sorrow.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Kurugsar warns that heavy snow and violent wind will threaten the legions, advising retreat; the people fear perishing like the companions of Kai-khosru under snow drifts.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Isfendiyr states he has overcome five perils and fears no remaining two; he says he will go alone if the others return, after which the people pledge not to forsake him.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Isfendiyr camps near a mountain with a running stream and pitches tents.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "A storm of wind and heavy snow covers the earth; the leader and soldiers take shelter in a caverned rock for three days; man and beast grow faint for want of food.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Isfendiyr and his warriors prostrate in prayer to the Almighty for protection; the snow and wind cease and the army leaves the mountain caves.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Kurugsar says the Brazen Fortress is forty farsangs away, is Arjsp's residence, and the road includes three farsangs where the sand is as hot as fire and there is no water; the fortress is said to have no visible path and to be beyond successful reduction even by a huge army.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4",
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Isfendiyr warns Kurugsar that if he is found lying he will be put to death; Kurugsar maintains his truthfulness and again advises returning because the seventh stage is beyond human strength.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    }
