  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "After Isfendiyr returns from conquest, Gushtsp celebrates him but delays fulfilling a prior promise to crown him. Isfendiyr consults his mother, then reproaches his father. Gushtsp seeks counsel from Jamsp about the stars, learns of Isfendiyr's high destiny, and then asks how the prince will die; a prophecy answers that a deadly dart from Rustem's bow will kill him.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Gushtsp orders Isfendiyr to continue governing the new empire, but permits him to return and instructs him to bring the booty and travel by the road of the Heft-khan.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "On the return route, Isfendiyr reaches a place of a previous winter-storm and finds property he had lost preserved under snowdrifts.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "A royal feast is held; Gushtsp repeatedly fills Isfendiyr's goblet with wine, both drink often, and both become intoxicated.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Gushtsp asks Isfendiyr to recount the Heft-khan expedition; Isfendiyr postpones the narration until the next day due to drunkenness, then provides a full account when sober.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Although pleased outwardly, Gushtsp feels envy and suspicion, described as writhing internally like a serpent, and he delays investing Isfendiyr with sovereignty despite a promise tied to Arjsp's overthrow.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Isfendiyr privately tells his mother Kitabn about Gushtsp's promise to crown him after he slew Arjsp and freed his sisters, and asks her to remind the king about faith and honor.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Kitabn advises Isfendiyr to keep silent, warns against imprisonment and chains, and counsels patience because succession and army favor him and his father is old and infirm.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Isfendiyr, suspecting his mother may speak to the king, addresses Gushtsp as if under the influence of wine and reproaches him for not fulfilling his promise.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Gushtsp replies that the throne is Isfendiyr's but is irritated; he consults Jamsp about what the stars foretell.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Jamsp prophesies Isfendiyr's exalted fortune and ultimate sovereignty over the \"seven climes\" (heft-aklm), which worsens Gushtsp's resentment; Gushtsp asks about Isfendiyr's death and a prophecy states he will be killed by a deadly dart from Rustem's bow.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    }
