  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "King Gushtsp feigns generosity toward his son Isfendiyr at a banquet, promising him crown and throne after Rustem is subdued, and urges him to kill or capture Rustem for alleged disloyalty. Isfendiyr protests, recalling past imprisonments, broken promises, and his Heft-khan trials and victories (monsters, enchantress, snow-storm, deep crossing, and the reduction of the Brazen Fortress), arguing he has earned the throne. Gushtsp insists and orders him to go bind Rustem and bring him captive; Isfendiyr remains reluctant, citing Rustem’s service to their ancestors and Gushtsp’s former hospitality with Rustem.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Gushtsp, pleased by news, says that if Isfendiyr had died at the Brazen Fortress he would not be facing a claim to the throne; he then resolves on a plan of dissimulation and orders a gorgeous banquet for relations and warriors.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "At the banquet Gushtsp publicly tells Isfendiyr that the crown and throne are his and praises him before the warriors.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Gushtsp claims Rustem refused aid in war against Arjsp, asserts Rustem boasts of principalities (Zabul, Kabul, Nim-ruz) and owing no allegiance, and proposes deputing Isfendiyr to put Rustem to death or bring him alive in bonds.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Nobles and heroes present approve Gushtsp’s proposed measure.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Gushtsp says he has sworn on the Zendavesta to relinquish power and place it in Isfendiyr’s hands as soon as Rustem is subdued, offering the empire’s resources for the task.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Isfendiyr replies by recalling that after defeating Arjsp earlier he was imprisoned and chained through Gurzam’s machinations, and he accuses Gushtsp of forgetting or disregarding promises.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Isfendiyr recounts Heft-khan exploits: slaying a wolf, a lion, and a dragon; punishing an enchantress; suffering a storm of snow; and crossing a vast deep securely.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Isfendiyr states he reduced the Brazen Fortress and laid Arjsp’s empire at Gushtsp’s feet, yet received neglect and scorn rather than reward.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Gushtsp remains unmoved but acknowledges the rebuke’s justice; he argues that nearly half of Iran is in Rustem’s possession and says he expects services from his son, described as having a form of brass and great valor.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Gushtsp directs Isfendiyr to go quickly, invade Rustem’s abode, bind his feet and hands in captive bands, and bring him to court so all may know Rustem is quelled.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Isfendiyr says he does not fear Rustem’s prowess and notes Rustem is old, but he expresses no wish to oppose him and reminds Gushtsp of Rustem’s past service to their ancestors and Gushtsp’s two years of hospitality with Rustem in Sistan.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Gushtsp insists that Rustem’s past service to ancestors is irrelevant to him and that Rustem’s refusal of aid is sufficient reason; Isfendiyr remains reluctant and implores Gushtsp to abandon the plan.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
