  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Rustem and Prince Isfendiyr quarrel: Isfendiyr insists he must bind Rustem according to Gushtsp’s command, while Rustem refuses and boasts of past deeds. They agree to drink and eat that day and fight the next morning. Rustem offers allegiance and suggests crowning Isfendiyr, but worries that killing the prince would stain his own name and accuses Gushtsp of a deceptive scheme. Isfendiyr rejects the plea and threatens Rustem; Rustem leaves on horseback.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Rustem claims he and his father supported Lohursp’s accession and says Gushtsp now shows ingratitude by wanting to bind him hand and foot.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Isfendiyr says he has come himself to fetter Rustem and grips and painfully wrings Rustem’s hand, surprising him.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "They postpone fighting: wine and refreshment are taken that day, and they plan to contend the next day with weapons; Isfendiyr states his first aim will be to bind Rustem and display him in fetters.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Rustem proposes that he will convey Isfendiyr to Zal, seat him on an ivory throne, place a golden crown on his head, open the treasury, and serve as his warrior-chief.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "At the meal Rustem eats rapidly and in great quantity and drinks multiple flagons of wine, astonishing Isfendiyr and the chiefs.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Isfendiyr tells Rustem to consult his father and warns that if Rustem will not accept being bound he will repent; Rustem invites Isfendiyr to come before sunrise to decide by battle.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Isfendiyr says he wants to meet Rustem and insists he must bind him; bringing him unfettered would let his father claim he could not put Rustem in bonds and would disgrace him.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Rustem says he fears a bad name if he kills Isfendiyr, calls the prince a “lovely branch” of an illustrious tree, and suggests Gushtsp is using a treacherous trick to urge Isfendiyr to death.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Isfendiyr rejects being deceived and repeats that Rustem must go in fetters; he tells Rustem to bring his father and brother to witness his downfall.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Rustem mounts his horse and hastens home.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    }
  ],
