  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Rustem insists on fighting Isfendiyr despite Zal's wish for reconciliation. Zal arms Rustem with grief and warns of ruin whether Rustem kills or is killed. Rustem prays and declares he wishes to take Isfendiyr alive. Rustem rides out alone and challenges Isfendiyr to single combat; both men refuse outside help and say they rely on God. They fight fiercely with successive weapons until both pause exhausted. During the lull, Zra provokes fighting between the armies; Nushwer challenges, kills Alwa, then is killed by Zra, after which the Iranian troops flee and many are slain, including Mehrns.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Rustem asks Zal for permission to fight Isfendiyr the next day; Zal recommends reconciliation, but Rustem says the fight is unavoidable due to insults and indignities.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Zal weeps, ties on Rustem's armor, and warns that killing Isfendiyr will make Rustem infamous, while Rustem's death would ruin Sistan.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Rustem tells Zal to trust in God, says he desires to take Isfendiyr alive and serve him rather than kill him.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Rustem arms himself and mounts Rakush; troops assemble; Zal assigns Zra to oversee the troops and assist Rustem if needed; Zal prostrates himself in prayer asking God for a prosperous day.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Bashtan initially thinks Rustem comes alone to offer peace, but Isfendiyr notes Rustem is armed; Rustem summons Isfendiyr from a high place; both instruct their armies to keep their distance, and both state they need no aid except God.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Rustem and Isfendiyr fight with javelins, spears, swords, and then battle-axes; both attempt to unhorse each other; they pause exhausted, with horses panting and covered with foam and blood, and armor rent.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
