    "summary": "As Rustem nears death, he asks Shughad to string his bow so his body will not be eaten by wild animals. Rustem uses the bow to shoot Shughad, piercing both a tree and the traitor. Rustem gives thanks to the Creator for enabling revenge and then dies. Other companions have already perished in pits prepared by the traitors; a survivor brings the news to Zal, who laments. Zal sends Fermurz to Kabul to recover Rustem; Fermurz finds only skeletons and gathers and buries the bones. Fermurz later captures the king of Kabul and has him executed at Sistan. Separately, Gushtasp, old and infirm, bequeaths the empire to Bahman and dies after a long reign.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
