  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Drb governs justly and rewards a washerman and his wife, instructing them to continue washing at the river in case another box with an infant floats downstream. Drb defeats an invading Arabian army and later defeats Failaks of Rm; peace is made when Failaks gives his daughter Nahd to Drb in marriage. Nahd’s offensive breath is cured by a fragrant herb, and she later conceives but secretly returns to her father and gives birth to a son. Failaks hides the child’s true paternity, claims him as his own, and names him Sikander, educating him under the sage Aristtals. Drb later has another son, Dr; after Drb dies, Dr reigns until Sikander becomes king of Rm and kills Dr in war after refusing tribute.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "After ascending the throne, Drb rules with humanity, justice, and benevolence and secures the happiness of his people.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Drb summons a washerman and the washerman’s wife, enriches them with gifts, and requires them not to abandon washing clothes at the river-side in case another box floating down the stream contains another infant.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "An Arabian army of one hundred thousand men under Shb invades; Drb fights for three days and three nights, and on the fourth morning Shb is slain and the battle ends.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Drb captures immense booty and many Arabian horses, strengthening state resources.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Drb defeats Failaks (Philip of Macedon), king of Rm; many are killed and women and children are carried into captivity; Failaks takes refuge in a fortress and sends an ambassador seeking peace.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Drb demands Failaks’s daughter Nahd as the sole peace term; Failaks agrees and sends her with presents; Drb marries her and takes her to Persia.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Nahd has offensive breath; a fragrant herb is found and used as a mouthwash, curing the problem.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "When Nahd becomes likely to be a mother, she does not tell Drb and asks permission to visit her father; in Rm she gives birth to a son.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Failaks, having no male offspring, keeps the birth unknown to Drb, publicly claims the child as his own, and the boy is called Sikander.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Sikander becomes accomplished in diplomacy and war; Failaks places him under Aristtals, and Sikander equals his master in learning and science.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Drb marries another wife and has a son named Dr; when Dr is twenty, Drb dies after reigning thirty-four years.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Dr continues governance and demands tribute; after Failaks dies, Sikander becomes king of Rm, refuses tribute, goes to war with Dr, and kills him in battle.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:11"
      ]
    }
