  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "After Dr’s army turns against him, he is defeated and flees; Sikander captures Dr’s wife and family but returns them. Two of Dr’s ministers, anticipating his capture, stab him at night to gain Sikander’s favor. Sikander finds the wounded Dr, weeps, calls him a brother, and promises vengeance on the murderers. Dying, Dr asks Sikander to preserve his family’s honor by marrying his daughter Roshung and, if he has a son, to name him Isfendiyr and uphold Zerdusht’s sacred doctrines (Zendavesta), keep the Nu-rz festival, and light the Holy Fire at the altar. Dr dies after a final gesture; Sikander buries him with honor and executes the two ministers. Sikander then rules Persia, fulfills the marriage request, and later sets out to conquer Ind.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
