      "text": "A note compares a passage to Plutarch’s account of Themistocles speaking to Xerxes: discourse is likened to a tapestry whose figures show when spread and hide when folded; Themistocles asks time and learns Persian within a year to speak without an interpreter.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "A note identifies Hujr as son of Gdarz and remarks that very large families among eastern princes are not rare; it cites a report that the King of Persia in 1809 had sixty-five sons.",
