    "summary": "A sequence of footnotes explains references in Persian poetry: Solomon’s vizier Asaf and a stolen magical signet ring; Majnun and Layla; images of tavern, tulip ‘brand of love,’ kings and prayer-direction; Korah swallowed by the earth; Solomon’s vanished splendor; Mount Qaf encircling the world; Moses and the valley where God appeared; kalandar dervishes; Zoroaster and fire-worship; the punished tribes ‘Ad and Thamud; the forbidden fruit as wheat; a deadly glance; and the ‘alif-form’ upright stature.",
